Hi, Jiufei,
Thanks for your response.

As we remove a file from the mount point, the issue is created random.
I search the position the variables is set with zero, and they are:
        ---- l_next_free_rec = 0 Matches (4 in 1 files) ----
        Alloc.c:2606:           el->l_next_free_rec = 0;
        Alloc.c:3120:           el->l_next_free_rec = 0;

The issue may be created when file is removed, and the space resource released.
The variables may be set with zero before the function of ocfs2_commit_truncate is called.
It may be some locks used appropriately when file removed, and resource released.
We reviewed the code and cannot found any way to avoid this issue.
Would you have any other ideas about it?
Thanks


